# R100/R102: the value and monotonicity contract of os_gettime_ns. The
# ns->timespec relationship itself (process-wide anchor, tv_nsec
# normalisation, signed differences) is already pinned by
# 34-nstime-to-timespec; this script pins what 34 does not: the conversion
# is exactly linear (+N ns in == +N ns out, including across the 1 s
# boundary), non-decreasing in the input, and anchored once per process, so
# converting the same pair of timestamps again yields the same difference.
# All printed differences are pure functions of the inputs (byte-stable).
nstime +0 +1000000
nstime +0 +1000000
nstime +1000000000 +1000000000
nstime +1000000 +2000000
nstime -2000000 -1000000
nstime +0 +1000000000
nstime +1000000000 +2000000000
